    "background_story": "Jason was a brilliant and eccentric scientist who had always been fascinated by the electrophorus, a device that generates static electricity. As a child, he spent hours watching videos of Benjamin Franklin's experiments with electricity. This curiosity led him to pursue a career in physics, focusing on the study of electrostatics. Jason's groundbreaking research on the electrophorus led to the development of a new, sustainable energy source. His invention, the 'ElectroGen', harnessed the power of static electricity to generate electricity, revolutionizing the field of renewable energy. Jason's work earned him international recognition, and he became known as the 'Electrophorus Whisperer'. His passion for the subject had sparked a new era in energy production, changing the world one spark at a time.",
